{
  "$comment": "Canonical permission rules for the untracked per-machine ~/.claude/settings.json (README 'settings.json' > permissions.ask). node scripts/sync-permissions.js merges them: every `ask` rule and its Bash(rtk ...) twin is added (the rtk hook rewrites git/gh commands and rules are matched against the rewritten command), `retireAsk` rules and their twins are removed, `forbidAllow` rules are removed from `allow`; other keys and local rules stay. Write rules in their base form only (no rtk prefix) and keep them narrow: combined short flags such as -uf, `git -C <dir> push` and `bash -c` strings are checked by scripts/guard-push-delete.js. Never write `:*` here — it is prefix-rule syntax (README guard-push-delete.js).",
